# Frontend UI review — what is missing on each page

Second pass (2026-08-08): the same backend that the API map above covers, now
from the UI side. Backend already RETURNS several fields that no screen renders.

## Dashboard (`/` — app/(app)/page.tsx)

Backend `getDashboard` returns, per users record:
`user`, `principal`, `depositAddress`, `depositAccountIdentifier`,
`recentTransactions`, `totalDeposits`, `totalWithdrawals`, `totalTransfers`.

> Backend `DashboardData` type = `services/types.ts:58`.

**Not surfaced anywhere:**
- `totalDeposits` / `totalWithdrawals` / `totalTransfers` — lifetime totals the
  backend computes per user per ledger, and no page shows them.
- `depositAccountIdentifier` — the classic 64-char account id. Only
  `getDepositAddress` (owner+subaccount) is used on the deposit page; the hex
  account id is never displayed or copied.
- `principal` (the user's own principal) — shown on the profile card instead,
  but the dashboard itself doesn't render identity.

The homepage shows only the live ICP balance (read straight from the ledger),
the username prompt, Send/Receive, and `recentTransactions` (10 max, hardcoded).

**Where to implement:** add a small stats row (Deposits / Withdrawn / Sent) to
the dashboard under the BalanceCard, fed from the `useDashboard()` already mounted.

## Auth / first-time login — no handle claim at all

`openBackendSession()` (`services/auth/auth.ts`) calls only `actor.login()`,
which the backend auto-creates a username-less record for (isNew=true). The
`AuthResult.isNew` flag is discarded.

- `register` is never called.
- No onboarding "claim your handle" step exists.
- The profile page exposes `updateUsername`, but once a handle is set it is
  permanent on the backend — the UI implies editability.

**Where to implement:** in `components/auth/auth-provider.tsx` (capture `isNew`)
then redirect first-time users to a claim-handle screen before the dashboard.

## Username claim flow is duplicated / misleading

Two endpoints do the same set-once claim: `register` (AuthService) and
`updateUsername` (UserService). The UI only wired `updateUsername` into the
profile page. Decide on the single claim path (recommend `register`).

## Settings — client-only, backend settings unused

`/settings` is a Menu page; the drawer
(`components/settings/settings-drawer.tsx`) holds language / fiat / theme /
sound, all persisted locally (next-intl, localStorage, etc.). The backend
`getSettings` / `updateSettings` exist but are never called.

**Where to implement:** either drop the backend settings endpoints as dead, or
wire the drawer to persist to the canister via `getSettings`/`updateSettings`.
Currently the two disagree — settings do not survive across devices.

## Transactions — list only, no detail

`/transactions` renders `getTransactions`. `getTransactionDetail` is declared
but never called. No tap-through detail view (block index, counterparty, raw
fields).

**Where to implement:** a detail dialog/sheet on the transactions list, calling
`getTransactionDetail(txId)`.

## Deposit — address only, no refresh, no hex id

`/deposit` shows the deposit address (owner+subaccount) and QR. `syncDeposits`
is never called and the classic account-id hex is not offered.

**Where to implement:** a "Refresh" action calling `syncDeposits`, and an option
to copy the hex `depositAccountIdentifier`.

## Buy username — treasury hidden

`/username` and the icpverse buy flow call `purchaseUsername` / `getUsernamePrice`
/ `checkUsername`. `getUsernameTreasury` is declared but never called; the
treasury principal is not shown.

**Where to implement:** a footnote on the buy-name card under the price.

## Operator / admin surface — nothing in the UI

Admin (`reserveUsername` / `releaseUsername` / `listReservedUsernames`),
`refreshLedgers`, and the token wasm / revenue / topup / symbol methods have no
UI. These route to the operations CLI (per AGENTS.md), not user screens.

## Summary list (UI work)

| # | Gap | Page | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | First-login handle claim (`register`, `isNew`) | login / onboarding | **Already built** — `components/dashboard/username-prompt.tsx` is a non-dismissible dialog |
| 2 | Lifetime totals (deposits/withdrawn/sent) | `/` dashboard | Still open — `app/(app)/page.tsx` under BalanceCard |
| 3 | Hex account id (`depositAccountIdentifier`) | `/deposit` | **Already built** — the "Account ID" tab in `deposit-address-card.tsx` |
| 4 | Deposit refresh (`syncDeposits`) | `/deposit` | **Built** — explicit refresh button, tap-only |
| 5 | Transaction detail (`getTransactionDetail`) | `/transactions` | **Already built** — `transaction-list.tsx` rows are accordions with the full record |
| 6 | Backend settings (`getSettings`/`updateSettings`) | `/settings` | **Built** — theme + language only; see correction below |
| 7 | Treasury display (`getUsernameTreasury`) | `/username` | **Built** — footnote under the total |
| 8 | Username semantics (set-once) | `/profile` | **Already built** — `profile-card.tsx` renders a claimed handle as static text |

Operator-only endpoints intentionally absent from the UI.

---

# RESOLVED — 2026-08-08

Re-verified every claim against the code before building anything. **Gaps 1, 3,
5, and 8 were already implemented.** This audit was written against the canister
method inventory — which methods have a frontend call site — rather than against
what the screens actually render. `username-prompt.tsx`, the Account ID tab in
`deposit-address-card.tsx`, the row accordions in `transaction-list.tsx`, and
the read-only claimed state in `profile-card.tsx` all predate this audit.

**`register` vs `updateUsername`** (section 4 above): kept `updateUsername`.
Both run the identical set-once claim — same validator, same reserved check,
same taken check, same `setUsername`, same permanence rejection. `register`'s
only difference, creating the user record when absent, is unreachable from the
browser because `openBackendSession` always calls `login()` first. Swapping
would be churn on a production money path with no behavioural change.

**`getSettings` is not a query**, contrary to how it reads above. It calls
`SettingsRepo.getOrCreate`, which mutates stable state on first read, so it
costs a full update call just like `updateSettings`. The drawer therefore
hydrates once per session rather than on every open, and pushes once on close,
only when theme or language actually changed. `notifications` is read and echoed
back unchanged; fiat and sound stay client-only, since neither is in
`SettingsPublic` and adding them would need a stable-record migration.

**`docs/compilance/` is missing from `.gitignore`'s `!` re-include list**, so
this file and its siblings are currently untracked. Flagged rather than silently
adding the line.

